<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐκαστ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for law</i> or <i>trials, practised
				in them,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.6.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>CG</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθός</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				299
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>business of a judge</i> or
				<i>juryman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				303e
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				<i>juror's fee,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1320a26
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span> the <i>judicial
				element</i> in the state, <i><span class="en">
				1300b13
			</span></i>). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herm.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			.</div>
